        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-08T15:01:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right, my naive assumption actually completely missed the fact that load-store instructions are not even able to express a pointer to the \"middle\" range to begin with!\n\nThis is due to the CPU selecting the appropriate `TTBRx_EL1` based on the MSB of the address operand then, depending on `TCR_EL1.TxSZ` (similarly selected), only looking at its `va_bits` LSBs to index the page tables, AFAIU. As a result, the non-sign MSBs above `va_bits` are NOT taken as address bits, making it impossible for SW to express a pointer to the \"middle\" VA range...\n\nI am tempted to use a `TTBR1` address instead, which will result in a translation fault as long as `TCR_EL1.EPD1` is not cleared, but am still thinking about how to assert this assumption so that it doesn\u0027t bitrot. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "c6b39009_dc881234",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 133,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "d4e0f5b58ecdcf704c4f4d6401ffc400adc459c5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5520768f_a75e94fa",
        "filename": "vmbase/src/bionic.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 133,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-08T15:15:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, if I\u0027m not mistaken, the addresses this patchset uses will remain invalid until vmbase starts using `TTBR1` **and** enables 52-bit addresses through `TCR_EL1.T1SZ`, right? How likely is this to actually bitrot...?\n\nI\u0027ve updated the commit message and code comment to reflect this; please LMK what you think.",
      "parentUuid": "60297b08_28bf954d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 133,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "d4e0f5b58ecdcf704c4f4d6401ffc400adc459c5",
